    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0710" n="672" xml:id="pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/8127½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary to the President</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tumulty</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-24">24 November, 1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Lansing</hi>: Mrs. Wilson this morning sent
                    me the following memorandum with regard to the matter contained in your letter
                    of the 21st instant to the President: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The President says he agrees with the Secretary as regards to
                            withdrawing our representatives in Paris, and of retaining our member of
                            the Supreme Council.</p>
                        <p>“About the signing of the Treaty with Bulgaria, he thinks if the American
                            representatives are still in Paris, they could sign, but does not advise
                            their remaining for that purpose.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. P. Tumulty</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
